        "content": "<p>jrandolf opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14852\">issue #14852</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wasmtime ignores the type ascription on component exports. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"WebAssembly\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">component</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">core</span> <span class=\"k\">module</span> <span class=\"nv\">$m</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"f\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"g\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"kt\">i32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"nb\">i32.const</span> <span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">core</span> <span class=\"err\">instance</span> <span class=\"nv\">$i</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">instantiate</span> <span class=\"nv\">$m</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$f</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"err\">u</span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">canon</span> <span class=\"err\">l</span><span class=\"nb\">if</span><span class=\"err\">t</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">core</span> <span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$i</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"f\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$g</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"err\">u</span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">canon</span> <span class=\"err\">l</span><span class=\"nb\">if</span><span class=\"err\">t</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">core</span> <span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$i</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"g\"</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">instance</span> <span class=\"nv\">$inst</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"f\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$f</span><span class=\"p\">))</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"g\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"nv\">$g</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n  <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"hidden\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">instance</span> <span class=\"nv\">$inst</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"err\">instance</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">export</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"f\"</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">func</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">result</span> <span class=\"err\">u</span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"p\">)))))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The ascription hides <code>g</code>, but <code>component_type()</code> still lists <code>g</code> under <code>hidden</code>, and the host can look it up with <code>Instance::get_export_index(Some(&amp;hidden), \"g\")</code> and call it (it returns 2). Attributes that come from the ascription, such as <code>(implements \"..\")</code> or <code>(external-id \"..\")</code> on a nested export, are lost as well, and the same item can report different attributes depending on which path it's exported through.</p>\n<p>It looks like <code>translate.rs</code> records <code>(item, name)</code> for exports and drops <code>export.ty</code>, and the root export types are then built from the definition rather than the ascribed type. Guests aren't affected; this is about what the embedder API exposes.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
