hat come from the ascription, such as <code>(implements \"..\")</code> or <code>(external-id \"..\")</code> on a nested export, are lost as well, and the same item can report different attributes depending on which path it's exported through.</p>\n<p>It looks like <code>translate.rs</code> records <code>(item, name)</code> for exports and drops <code>export.ty</code>, and the root export types are then built from the definition rather than the ascribed type. Guests aren't affected; this is about what the embedder API exposes.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
